(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The threaded way (HES84 (a), doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md \"As built: HES84 (a), the threaded way\"): a program GHC"] [10 1 "// links -threaded (hsi run --threaded) runs with the threaded RTS's semantics where a program can observe them, staged:"] [11 1 "//   - capabilities: enabled_capabilities is +RTS -N's (default 1), setNumCapabilities changes it (clamped to the larger of -N"] [12 1 "//     and the host's processors, as Capability.c's max_n_capabilities), forkOn's capability is its number modulo it; the"] [13 1 "//     Haskell threads are still evaluated by one goroutine, the capability every thread runs on in turn (stage 1: no two"] [14 1 "//     Haskell threads in parallel, which no judged output depends on);"] [15 1 "//   - safe foreign calls release the capability (Schedule.c's suspendThread and resumeThread): a safe call to a host function"] [16 1 "//     that only blocks (sleep, usleep, nanosleep) runs on a goroutine of its own while the other threads run, its thread"] [17 1 "//     BlockedOnCCall until it returns; an asynchronous exception thrown to it waits for the return, as GHC's (a non-interruptible"] [18 1 "//     call). Unsafe calls, and safe calls into the program's own C (ci's interpreter is the machine's), keep the capability;"] [19 1 "//   - bound threads: the main thread, forkOS's (forkOS_createThread) and the in-calls' threads are bound"] [20 1 "//     (isCurrentThreadBound#); rtsSupportsBoundThreads answers 1 to GHC.Internal.Conc.Bound and the program's own modules, and"] [21 1 "//     0 to the I/O manager's modules (GHC.Internal.Conc.IO's threadDelay and threadWaitRead, IO.FD, System.Timeout, the"] [22 1 "//     signals): the I/O manager stays hsi's own, the non-threaded RTS's awaitEvent over delay#, waitRead# and waitWrite# (the"] [23 1 "//     threaded RTS's Haskell event manager over epoll is not ported: the same waits, by another mechanism);"] [24 1 "//   - sparks: a pool of at most 4096 (GHC's maxLocalSparks) unevaluated closures, numSparks# its size; an idle scheduler runs"] [25 1 "//     them one at a time, as an idle capability's spark thread;"] [26 1 "//   - hs_exit (and the end of main): the standard handles flushed, then exitScheduler's shutdown: the other threads deleted,"] [27 1 "//     those in foreign calls left to return into a stopped RTS (their goroutines' results dropped)."] [29 1 "// fcall is a safe foreign call in flight on a goroutine of its own: its thread blocked on it until done is sent."] [32 13 "// the result's representation"] [33 13 "// the result, set by the goroutine before it is sent"] [34 2 "// after runs on the machine's goroutine when the call has returned (a result written to memory)"] [38 1 "// blockingCall is a host function a safe call may run off the machine: its arguments read on the machine's goroutine"] [39 1 "// (prepare), the blocking part on another (run), what it writes back on the machine's again (after, may be nil)."] [66 1 "// offload starts a safe foreign call of a blocking host function on a goroutine and blocks the current thread on it; ok"] [67 1 "// false when the call is not one (the caller makes it on the machine)."] [87 1 "// callReturned resumes a thread whose foreign call returned (resumeThread): its result in its return registers, an"] [88 1 "// exception thrown to it meanwhile raised now that it accepts one."] [96 10 "// deleted at shutdown (exitScheduler): the call returned into a stopped RTS"] [113 1 "// drainCalls resumes the threads whose calls have returned, without waiting."] [125 1 "// waitCall waits for a foreign call to return, at most d (d < 0: no limit); whether one did."] [142 1 "// ---- capabilities ----"] [144 1 "// maxCaps is max_n_capabilities: the larger of -N and the host's processors."] [149 1 "// setNumCapabilities is the RTS's (Schedule.c): the non-threaded RTS refuses any count but 1."] [174 1 "// caps is enabled_capabilities."] [182 1 "// SetCapabilities is +RTS -N's count (the threaded way's; 0: the default, 1)."] [190 1 "// capOf is the capability a thread is on: a locked thread's (forkOn's number modulo the count), else 0 (hsi's one"] [191 1 "// evaluator runs every thread on the first capability)."] [199 1 "// ---- sparks ----"] [203 1 "// spark adds a closure to the pool (newSpark): only an unevaluated one (an evaluated one fizzles, a dud), dropped when"] [204 1 "// the pool is full (an overflow); the non-threaded RTS has no pool."] [219 1 "// nextSpark is the oldest spark still unevaluated, taken from the pool (findSpark: the fizzled ones dropped), or nil."] [233 1 "// runSpark starts a thread evaluating the next spark when the scheduler is idle (an idle capability's spark thread);"] [234 1 "// whether it did."] [244 1 "// ---- bound threads ----"] [246 1 "// forkOSCreate is forkOS_createThread(entry): a bound thread running the IO action the stable pointer entry names"] [247 1 "// (OSThreads.c's forkOS_createThreadWrapper, rts_evalStableIO), 0 (success)."] [260 1 "// ---- shutdown ----"] [262 1 "// exitScheduler is the threaded RTS's shutdown after the handles are flushed: every other thread deleted (no handler"] [263 1 "// runs), those in foreign calls left to return into a stopped RTS."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[45 38] [49 38] [57 38] [105 26] [164 22]] :go/trails [[63 3]]} (go/file "threaded.go" :imports [


